WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.160
COUNCIL OF MINISTERS

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:03.880
LEGISLATES ON BEHALF OF
THE NATIONAL GOVERNMENTS

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:11.800
The councils are the main legislative
bodies of the European Union.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:15.160
It is, kind of,
the 27 Member States' house.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:19.000
It is where ministers
from each country meet.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:25.480
The Council of Ministers
meets in various formations.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:32.640
In each case, the ministers responsible
for specific fields take part.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:37.200
When a compromise is made, on the
basis of a proposal from the Commission,

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:39.640
we will negotiate
with the European Parliament.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:43.680
Our role, my role as
President of the Council,

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:48.960
is more of a facilitator, a mediator.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:52.520
Our aim is to reach a consensus.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:54.280
It is a challenge.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:57.120
You are chairing a meeting
in another language

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:01.640
and some of the issues that we are
debating are of a very complex nature.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:08.600
The most difficult part is what is
required before you sit at the table,

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:12.400
so good preparation is essential.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:16.760
You have personal contact
with each member of the Council.

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:23.240
Knowing the background
of each one's position is important.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:27.400
So you get to know
the "whys" and the "whats".

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:32.800
I think it is very important
that you hear what other people say.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:34.760
That you really listen.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:38.520
Not just give them the floor and
say thank you, but you really listen.

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:41.800
Understanding the others' position

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:47.960
is a key element in reaching decisions
on a European level.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:53.360
There has been a lot of fuss and worry
and debate about Europe in general,

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:55.200
but Europe is also working.

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:57.040
We can take decisions.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:02.280
We can throw light on the way
some financial products are traded.

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:07.720
We can make sure that we handle
a foreign policy situation.

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:10.400
We can deal with
farming and agriculture,

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:13.720
environment and climate,
energy efficiency.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.840
We take decisions. This will be
better for the citizens in the future.

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:21.560
Because it is important that the Union
works regardless of the crisis,

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:25.760
regardless of the debates about
Europe's global standing.

